# PostgreSQL liveness — every minute
#
# Deliberately does NOT use `op run` — resolving secrets from 1Password at
# per-minute frequency gets rate-limited and silently kills the monitor (this
# happened in prod). Env instead comes from /etc/vps/pg-health.env, a
# plaintext file seeded from 1Password by `make cron-env-seed`
# (scripts/seed-cron-env.sh, template cron/pg-health.env.tpl). If it hasn't
# been seeded yet, sourcing a missing file fails loudly (bash logs the error
# to pg-health.log below) rather than silently degrading.
#
# Install: installed automatically by scripts/setup.sh (section 12).
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin

* * * * * jkrumm /bin/bash -c 'set -a; . /etc/vps/pg-health.env; set +a; /home/jkrumm/vps/scripts/health-pg.sh' >> /home/jkrumm/pg-health.log 2>&1
